IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `colc-common`
IMPORT `colc-concessions`

-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website (State of South Australia, CC BY 4.0), taken
-- from the Open Australian Legal Corpus (CC BY 4.0); each text may be out of date.
--
-- Cases for colc-concessions.l4: the Cost of Living Concessions Act 1986 and Regulations 2020. Every expected value is
-- worked by hand from the deposited text, with the arithmetic in the comment above the assertion. People, amounts,
-- incomes and CPI figures are ILLUSTRATIVE (no ABS figure or Minister's notice is deposited).
--
-- A breached or still-pending DEONTIC cannot be asserted on the stable l4, so regulative rules are asserted where the
-- trace ends FULFILLED, and #TRACEd with an "-- expect:" line where it does not. Clock: days.

§ `Cases -- cost of living concession and water rates remission`

§§ `Shared helpers`

#ASSERT `rounded up to the nearest 10 cents` 263.117 EQUALS 263.2
#ASSERT `rounded up to the nearest 10 cents` 255.6 EQUALS 255.6
#ASSERT `days from` (YearMonthDay 2024 7 1) `to` (YearMonthDay 2024 12 30) EQUALS 182
-- 31 January 2024 plus one month: February 2024 has 29 days.
#ASSERT DATE_SERIAL (`one month after` (YearMonthDay 2024 1 31)) EQUALS DATE_SERIAL (YearMonthDay 2024 2 29)
#ASSERT DATE_SERIAL (`one month after` (YearMonthDay 2024 12 15)) EQUALS DATE_SERIAL (YearMonthDay 2025 1 15)

§§ `s 2(2), (3), reg 3(2), reg 4 -- owner or tenant`

`Margaret's home` MEANS `Occupation of premises` WITH
    `the premises are occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes` IS TRUE
    `the premises are the person's principal place of residence` IS TRUE
    `the capacity` IS `as a sole or joint proprietor of an estate in freehold in possession`

`Josh's flat` MEANS `Occupation of premises` WITH
    `the premises are occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes` IS TRUE
    `the premises are the person's principal place of residence` IS TRUE
    `the capacity` IS `as a tenant specified in a residential tenancy agreement`

`Priya's room` MEANS `Occupation of premises` WITH
    `the premises are occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes` IS TRUE
    `the premises are the person's principal place of residence` IS TRUE
    `the capacity` IS `as a rooming house resident under a rooming house agreement`

`Tom's parents' house` MEANS `Occupation of premises` WITH
    `the premises are occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes` IS TRUE
    `the premises are the person's principal place of residence` IS TRUE
    `the capacity` IS `in none of these capacities`

`Ruth's park site` MEANS `Occupation of premises` WITH
    `the premises are occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes` IS TRUE
    `the premises are the person's principal place of residence` IS TRUE
    `the capacity` IS `under a right of occupancy under a residential park site agreement`

`Margaret's holiday shack` MEANS `Occupation of premises` WITH
    `the premises are occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes` IS TRUE
    `the premises are the person's principal place of residence` IS FALSE
    `the capacity` IS `as a sole or joint proprietor of an estate in freehold in possession`

`the shop with a flat` MEANS `Occupation of premises` WITH
    `the premises are occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes` IS FALSE
    `the premises are the person's principal place of residence` IS TRUE
    `the capacity` IS `as a sole or joint proprietor of an estate in freehold in possession`

-- Ann lives, as her principal place of residence, in the house her husband is entitled to occupy as a beneficiary
-- under his mother's estate.
`Ann, living in her husband's inherited home` MEANS `Occupation of premises` WITH
    `the premises are occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes` IS TRUE
    `the premises are the person's principal place of residence` IS TRUE
    `the capacity` IS `as the spouse or domestic partner of a beneficiary under an estate`

-- s 2(2)(a), (b)(i): freehold proprietor, principal place of residence.
#ASSERT `the way the person occupies the premises` `Margaret's home` EQUALS `as an owner`
-- s 2(3)(b)(i).
#ASSERT `the way the person occupies the premises` `Josh's flat` EQUALS `as a tenant`
-- s 2(3)(b)(ii), reg 4(2)(b).
#ASSERT `the way the person occupies the premises` `Priya's room` EQUALS `as a tenant`
-- Living in someone else's home with no listed capacity.
#ASSERT `the way the person occupies the premises` `Tom's parents' house` EQUALS `neither as an owner nor as a tenant`
-- s 2(2)(b)(ix), reg 4(1)(b): a residential park site agreement makes an owner for the concession ...
#ASSERT `the way the person occupies the premises` `Ruth's park site` EQUALS `as an owner`
-- ... but it is not a reg 3(2) prescribed capacity for the water rates remission.
#ASSERT NOT (`the person occupies the land as principal place of residence in a prescribed capacity` `Ruth's park site`)
#ASSERT `the person occupies the land as principal place of residence in a prescribed capacity` `Margaret's home`
-- s 2(2)(a): not the principal place of residence.
#ASSERT `the way the person occupies the premises` `Margaret's holiday shack` EQUALS `neither as an owner nor as a tenant`
-- s 2(1) "residential premises": occupied solely or primarily for residential purposes.
#ASSERT `the way the person occupies the premises` `the shop with a flat` EQUALS `neither as an owner nor as a tenant`
-- reg 3(2)(h), reg 4(1)(a): an owner's spouse is in both.
#ASSERT `is an owner's capacity under section 2(2)(b)` `as the spouse or domestic partner of a person occupying in one of the capacities above other than as a beneficiary under an estate`
#ASSERT `is a prescribed capacity under regulation 3(2)` `as the spouse or domestic partner of a person occupying in one of the capacities above other than as a beneficiary under an estate`
-- s 2(2)(b)(viii), reg 3(2)(i): a beneficiary under an estate is in both ...
#ASSERT `is an owner's capacity under section 2(2)(b)` `as a beneficiary under an estate entitling me to occupy in one of the capacities above`
#ASSERT `is a prescribed capacity under regulation 3(2)` `as a beneficiary under an estate entitling me to occupy in one of the capacities above`
-- ... but the beneficiary's spouse is in neither: reg 4(1)(a) reaches spouses of persons in s 2(2)(b)(i)-(vii) and reg
-- 3(2)(h) spouses of persons in (a)-(g), and the beneficiary is (viii) and (i) (finding 22).
#ASSERT NOT (`is an owner's capacity under section 2(2)(b)` `as the spouse or domestic partner of a beneficiary under an estate`)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a prescribed capacity under regulation 3(2)` `as the spouse or domestic partner of a beneficiary under an estate`)
#ASSERT `the way the person occupies the premises` `Ann, living in her husband's inherited home` EQUALS `neither as an owner nor as a tenant`
#ASSERT NOT (`the person occupies the land as principal place of residence in a prescribed capacity` `Ann, living in her husband's inherited home`)

§§ `reg 3(1), reg 6 -- the prescribed classes`

