§§ `s 3(2), reg 7 -- entitlement`

-- A claim builder, so each case states only what differs.
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paid last year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `ADI details` IS A BOOLEAN
      `someone else paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `same room` IS A BOOLEAN
      `split approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Concession claim`
`a claim for` `the year` `applied` `paid last year` `ADI details` `someone else paid` `same room` `split approved` MEANS
    `Concession claim` WITH
        `the financial year begins in` IS `the year`
        `applied to the Minister before 31 December in the financial year` IS `applied`
        `was paid the concession for the previous financial year for the same premises` IS `paid last year`
        `the Minister has been provided with ADI account details for payment` IS `ADI details`
        `another eligible person has been paid for the financial year for the same premises` IS `someone else paid`
        `that other eligible person is a resident in the same room` IS `same room`
        `the Minister has approved splitting the payment with the other eligible person` IS `split approved`
        `entered the Switch for Solar program` IS FALSE
        `the financial year in which the Switch for Solar program was entered begins in` IS 0
        `received a payment for the financial year in which the Switch for Solar program was entered` IS FALSE
        `the Minister has determined that exceptional circumstances lift the Switch for Solar bar for this financial year` IS FALSE

-- A claim from someone who entered Switch for Solar in the financial year beginning in `entered in`.
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `entered in` IS A NUMBER
      `paid for that year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `exceptional circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Concession claim`
`a Switch for Solar claim for` `the year` `entered in` `paid for that year` `exceptional circumstances` MEANS
    `Concession claim` WITH
        `the financial year begins in` IS `the year`
        `applied to the Minister before 31 December in the financial year` IS TRUE
        `was paid the concession for the previous financial year for the same premises` IS FALSE
        `the Minister has been provided with ADI account details for payment` IS TRUE
        `another eligible person has been paid for the financial year for the same premises` IS FALSE
        `that other eligible person is a resident in the same room` IS FALSE
        `the Minister has approved splitting the payment with the other eligible person` IS FALSE
        `entered the Switch for Solar program` IS TRUE
        `the financial year in which the Switch for Solar program was entered begins in` IS `entered in`
        `received a payment for the financial year in which the Switch for Solar program was entered` IS `paid for that year`
        `the Minister has determined that exceptional circumstances lift the Switch for Solar bar for this financial year` IS `exceptional circumstances`

-- Margaret applied in time, gave her account details, and no one else was paid for her home.
`Margaret's 2024/25 claim` MEANS `a claim for` 2024 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- s 3(2): eligible, applied before 31 December (reg 7(1)(a)), ADI details (b), no one else paid (c).
#ASSERT `the person's entitlement to the concession` `Margaret on 1 July 2024` `Margaret's 2024/25 claim` EQUALS `entitled to the concession`
-- reg 7(2): no application needed when paid last year for the same premises.
#ASSERT `the person's entitlement to the concession` `Margaret on 1 July 2024` (`a claim for` 2024 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `entitled to the concession`
-- reg 7(1)(a): neither applied nor paid last year.
#ASSERT `the person's entitlement to the concession` `Margaret on 1 July 2024` (`a claim for` 2024 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `not entitled` `I did not apply before 31 December and was not paid last year for the same premises`
-- reg 7(1)(b).
#ASSERT `the person's entitlement to the concession` `Margaret on 1 July 2024` (`a claim for` 2024 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `not entitled` `the Minister has not been given my ADI account details`
-- reg 7(1)(c): another eligible person already paid for the same house.
#ASSERT `the person's entitlement to the concession` `Margaret on 1 July 2024` (`a claim for` 2024 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `not entitled` `another eligible person has been paid this year for the same premises`
-- reg 7(3aa): ... unless the Minister approves a split.
#ASSERT `the person's entitlement to the concession` `Margaret on 1 July 2024` (`a claim for` 2024 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `entitled to the share of the concession the Minister has approved under regulation 7(3aa)`
-- reg 7(3): a rooming house resident is not shut out by another resident's payment, unless in the same room.
#ASSERT `the person's entitlement to the concession` `Priya on 1 July 2024` (`a claim for` 2024 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `entitled to the concession`
#ASSERT `the person's entitlement to the concession` `Priya on 1 July 2024` (`a claim for` 2024 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `not entitled` `another eligible person has been paid this year for the same premises`
-- The same-room exception is for reg 4(2)(b), (c) residents only: a tenant under a residential tenancy agreement is
-- shut out.
#ASSERT `the person's entitlement to the concession` `Josh on 1 July 2024` (`a claim for` 2024 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `not entitled` `another eligible person has been paid this year for the same premises`
-- s 3(1)(a) fails first for Tom; reg 6 fails for Carl.
#ASSERT `the person's entitlement to the concession` `Tom on 1 July 2024` `Margaret's 2024/25 claim` EQUALS `not entitled` `not an eligible person: on 1 July I did not occupy residential premises as an owner or tenant`
#ASSERT `the person's entitlement to the concession` `Carl, renting on a wage above the limit` `Margaret's 2024/25 claim` EQUALS `not entitled` `not an eligible person: on 1 July I was not of a prescribed class`
-- Before 2024/25 the deposited reg 8 did not yet apply.
#ASSERT `the person's entitlement to the concession` `Margaret on 1 July 2024` (`a claim for` 2023 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `not covered: the deposited regulations apply from the 2024/2025 financial year`

-- reg 7(3a): entered Switch for Solar in 2022/23 and was paid for 2022/23: barred 2022/23 and the 10 following years,
-- 2023/24 to 2032/33; free again from 2033/34.
#ASSERT `the last financial year barred by Switch for Solar begins in` (`a Switch for Solar claim for` 2024 2022 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS 2032
#ASSERT `the person's entitlement to the concession` `Margaret on 1 July 2024` (`a Switch for Solar claim for` 2024 2022 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `not entitled` `the Switch for Solar program bars me this year`
#ASSERT `the person is barred by the Switch for Solar program` (`a Switch for Solar claim for` 2032 2022 TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is barred by the Switch for Solar program` (`a Switch for Solar claim for` 2033 2022 TRUE FALSE))
-- (3a)(b)(ii): not paid for 2022/23, so 9 following years: last barred 2031/32.
#ASSERT `the last financial year barred by Switch for Solar begins in` (`a Switch for Solar claim for` 2024 2022 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 2031
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is barred by the Switch for Solar program` (`a Switch for Solar claim for` 2032 2022 FALSE FALSE))
-- Either way ten financial years go without a payment: paid for 2022/23, then 2023/24 to 2032/33 (10) barred; or
-- 2022/23 to 2031/32 (10) barred (finding 5).
-- The year before entering is not barred.
#ASSERT NOT (`the person is barred by the Switch for Solar program` (`a Switch for Solar claim for` 2021 2022 TRUE FALSE))
-- (3a)(a): the first year barred is the year entered, 2022/23; with (b)(i) the span is 2022/23 to 2032/33, with (b)(ii)
-- 2022/23 to 2031/32.
#ASSERT `the first financial year barred by Switch for Solar begins in` (`a Switch for Solar claim for` 2024 2022 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS 2022
#ASSERT `the financial years barred by Switch for Solar` (`a Switch for Solar claim for` 2024 2022 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `barred for the financial years beginning in` 2022 2032
#ASSERT `the financial years barred by Switch for Solar` (`a Switch for Solar claim for` 2024 2022 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `barred for the financial years beginning in` 2022 2031
-- A (3c) determination lifts the bar for one particular year; it does not move the span.
#ASSERT `the financial years barred by Switch for Solar` (`a Switch for Solar claim for` 2024 2022 TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `barred for the financial years beginning in` 2022 2032
#ASSERT `the financial years barred by Switch for Solar` `Margaret's 2024/25 claim` EQUALS `not barred: the Switch for Solar program was not entered`
-- (3c): the Minister's exceptional circumstances determination lifts the bar for the year.
#ASSERT `the person's entitlement to the concession` `Margaret on 1 July 2024` (`a Switch for Solar claim for` 2024 2022 TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `entitled to the concession`

-- reg 7(1)(a): "before 31 December": the last day is 30 December 2024.
#ASSERT DATE_SERIAL (`the last day to apply for the concession for the financial year beginning in` 2024) EQUALS DATE_SERIAL (YearMonthDay 2024 12 30)
-- reg 7(2): paid for the previous year for the same premises lifts the requirement; otherwise it stands.
#ASSERT `regulation 7(2) lifts the application requirement` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 7(2) lifts the application requirement` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the application deadline for the financial year beginning in` 2024 FALSE EQUALS `apply on or before` (YearMonthDay 2024 12 30)
#ASSERT `the application deadline for the financial year beginning in` 2025 FALSE EQUALS `apply on or before` (YearMonthDay 2025 12 30)
#ASSERT `the application deadline for the financial year beginning in` 2024 TRUE EQUALS `no application needed: paid the concession for the previous financial year for the same premises`
#ASSERT `the application deadline for the financial year beginning in` 2023 FALSE EQUALS `not covered: the deposited regulations apply from the 2024/2025 financial year`

§§ `reg 3(3), (4), reg 8 -- the amount`

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER, `CPI before` IS A NUMBER, `CPI 2023` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Indexation figures`
`figures for` `the year` `CPI before` `CPI 2023` MEANS
    `Indexation figures` WITH
        `the financial year begins in` IS `the year`
        `the CPI for the December quarter of the year before the financial year begins` IS `CPI before`
        `the CPI for the December quarter of 2023` IS `CPI 2023`

-- 2024/25: multiplier 1; $255.60.
#ASSERT `the concession amount for the financial year` (`figures for` 2024 136 136) 0 EQUALS 255.60
-- For 2024/25 the multiplier is 1 even if two different December 2023 figures are typed in.
#ASSERT `the concession amount for the financial year` (`figures for` 2024 150 136) 0 EQUALS 255.60
-- reg 3(4): never below last year's amount (an illustrative $260).
#ASSERT `the concession amount for the financial year` (`figures for` 2024 136 136) 260 EQUALS 260
-- 2025/26, illustrative CPI December 2024 quarter 140, December 2023 quarter 136:
-- 255.60 x 140 / 136 = 35784 / 136 = 263.1176...; rounded up to 10 cents: 263.20.
#ASSERT `the concession amount for the financial year` (`figures for` 2025 140 136) 255.60 EQUALS 263.20
-- CPI fell to an illustrative 130: 255.60 x 130 / 136 = 33228 / 136 = 244.3235...; rounded up 244.40, below last
-- year's 255.60, so 255.60.
#ASSERT `the concession amount for the financial year` (`figures for` 2025 130 136) 255.60 EQUALS 255.60
-- Water remission minimum and maximum for 2025/26 on the same figures: 236.40 x 140 / 136 = 33096 / 136 = 243.3529...
-- -> 243.40; 377.00 x 140 / 136 = 52780 / 136 = 388.0882... -> 388.10.
#ASSERT `the indexed amount` `the prescribed minimum remission stated in regulation 5(5)` (`figures for` 2025 140 136) 236.40 EQUALS 243.40
#ASSERT `the indexed amount` `the prescribed maximum remission stated in regulation 5(5)` (`figures for` 2025 140 136) 377.00 EQUALS 388.10

§§ `s 4, reg 5 -- water rates remission`

GIVEN `rates` IS A NUMBER
      `share` IS A NUMBER
      `lives there in a prescribed capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `spouse lives there` IS A BOOLEAN
      `card when billed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `card when payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `spouse's card when billed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `spouse's card when payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `entitled last period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `hardship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Water rates position`
`water rates of` `rates` `share` `lives there in a prescribed capacity` `spouse lives there` `card when billed` `card when payable` `spouse's card when billed` `spouse's card when payable` `entitled last period` `hardship` MEANS
    `Water rates position` WITH
        `the water rates for the land for the financial year` IS `rates`
        `the ratepayer's proportion of interest in the land` IS `share`
        `the ratepayer occupies the land as principal place of residence in a prescribed capacity` IS `lives there in a prescribed capacity`
        `the spouse or domestic partner also occupies the land as principal place of residence` IS `spouse lives there`
        `the ratepayer holds a prescribed card or receives prescribed payments on the date billed` IS `card when billed`
        `the ratepayer holds a prescribed card or receives prescribed payments on the date payable` IS `card when payable`
        `the spouse or domestic partner holds a prescribed card or receives prescribed payments on the date billed` IS `spouse's card when billed`
        `the spouse or domestic partner holds a prescribed card or receives prescribed payments on the date payable` IS `spouse's card when payable`
        `the ratepayer was entitled to a remission of water rates for the preceding rating period` IS `entitled last period`
        `the Minister is satisfied by a means test that the ratepayer suffers exceptional circumstances of hardship` IS `hardship`

-- Margaret, sole owner living there, pensioner concession card on both dates, irrigation rates $1,000 (illustrative).
-- Arguments: rates, share, lives there in a prescribed capacity, spouse lives there, card when billed, card when
-- payable, spouse's card when billed, spouse's card when payable, entitled last period, hardship.
`Margaret's irrigation rates` MEANS `water rates of` 1000 1 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- reg 5(1)(a).
#ASSERT `the ratepayer meets the regulation 5 criteria for a remission of water rates` `Margaret's irrigation rates`
#ASSERT NOT (`the ratepayer meets the regulation 5 criteria for a remission of water rates` (`water rates of` 1000 1 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- reg 5(1)(b): the spouse's card, both living there.
#ASSERT `the ratepayer meets the regulation 5 criteria for a remission of water rates` (`water rates of` 1000 1 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- ... but not if the spouse lives elsewhere.
#ASSERT NOT (`the ratepayer meets the regulation 5 criteria for a remission of water rates` (`water rates of` 1000 1 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- reg 5(2): card on the payable date only: entitled only if entitled for the preceding rating period.
#ASSERT NOT (`the ratepayer meets the regulation 5 criteria for a remission of water rates` (`water rates of` 1000 1 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `the ratepayer meets the regulation 5 criteria for a remission of water rates` (`water rates of` 1000 1 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Card on the billing date only: reg 5(1)(a) on that relevant date; reg 5(2) does not apply.
#ASSERT `the ratepayer meets the regulation 5 criteria for a remission of water rates` (`water rates of` 1000 1 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- reg 5(1)(c): hardship on the Minister's means test, living there in a prescribed capacity.
#ASSERT `the ratepayer meets the regulation 5 criteria for a remission of water rates` (`water rates of` 1000 1 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the ratepayer meets the regulation 5 criteria for a remission of water rates` (`water rates of` 1000 1 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE))

-- reg 5(4), 2024/25 minimum 236.40 and maximum 377.00: rates 1000 x 30% = 300.
#ASSERT `the ratepayer's remission of water rates` `Margaret's irrigation rates` 236.40 377.00 EQUALS 300
-- rates 500 x 30% = 150, below the minimum: 236.40.
#ASSERT `the ratepayer's remission of water rates` (`water rates of` 500 1 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) 236.40 377.00 EQUALS 236.40
-- rates 2000 x 30% = 600, above the maximum: 377.00.
#ASSERT `the ratepayer's remission of water rates` (`water rates of` 2000 1 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) 236.40 377.00 EQUALS 377.00
-- rates 200: the minimum 236.40 is more than the rates; READING: the whole 200 (finding 11).
#ASSERT `the ratepayer's remission of water rates` (`water rates of` 200 1 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) 236.40 377.00 EQUALS 200
-- reg 5(3): a half share of land with rates 1000: 300 x 0.5 = 150.
#ASSERT `the ratepayer's remission of water rates` (`water rates of` 1000 0.5 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) 236.40 377.00 EQUALS 150
-- Not meeting the criteria: nothing.
#ASSERT `the ratepayer's remission of water rates` (`water rates of` 1000 1 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) 236.40 377.00 EQUALS 0

§§ `s 7, s 8 -- interest, penalties and debts`

#ASSERT `the interest, fine or penalty payable on rates remitted` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the interest the Minister pays on a concession` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the maximum penalty under section 8(2) or (3)` EQUALS 2500
-- s 8(4): a payment not due is recoverable in full ...
#ASSERT `the amount recoverable as a debt due to the Minister` 255.60 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 255.60
-- ... nothing if it was due ...
#ASSERT `the amount recoverable as a debt due to the Minister` 255.60 TRUE FALSE EQUALS 0
-- ... and nothing under reg 7(3b) where the payment came before entering Switch for Solar that year (finding 6).
#ASSERT `the amount recoverable as a debt due to the Minister` 255.60 FALSE TRUE EQUALS 0

§§ `Regulative rules`

-- reg 7(1)(a): 182 days from 1 July 2024 to 30 December 2024.
#ASSERT `the days from 1 July to the last day to apply` 2024 EQUALS 182
-- Margaret applies on 15 September 2024 (day 76) and is paid $255.60 on day 120.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`reg 7(1)(a), (2) -- apply before 31 December, unless paid last year for the same premises; then the Minister must pay` 2024 FALSE 255.60) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person` `apply to the Minister for the concession` 76), (EVENT `the Minister` (`pay the concession` 255.60) 120)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Applying on 30 December (day 182) is in time.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`reg 7(1)(a), (2) -- apply before 31 December, unless paid last year for the same premises; then the Minister must pay` 2024 FALSE 255.60) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person` `apply to the Minister for the concession` 182), (EVENT `the Minister` (`pay the concession` 255.60) 200)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Not applying is no breach: the concession is simply not payable.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`reg 7(1)(a), (2) -- apply before 31 December, unless paid last year for the same premises; then the Minister must pay` 2024 FALSE 255.60) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 183)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- reg 7(2): paid last year for the same home: the Minister must pay without an application.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`reg 7(1)(a), (2) -- apply before 31 December, unless paid last year for the same premises; then the Minister must pay` 2024 TRUE 255.60) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Minister` (`pay the concession` 255.60) 30)) EQUALS FULFILLED

#TRACE `reg 7(1)(a), (2) -- apply before 31 December, unless paid last year for the same premises; then the Minister must pay` 2024 FALSE 255.60 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person` DOES `apply to the Minister for the concession` AT 76
-- expect: the Minister's obligation still pending: PARTY `the Minister` MUST `pay the concession` 255.6 (s 3(2) sets no time)

#TRACE `reg 7(1)(a), (2) -- apply before 31 December, unless paid last year for the same premises; then the Minister must pay` 2024 FALSE 255.60 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person` DOES `apply to the Minister for the concession` AT 76
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `pay the concession` 200 AT 120
-- expect: still pending: a payment of 200 is not the 255.60 owed

-- s 8(2): told the Minister in writing within the (illustrative) 30 days.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 8(2) -- tell the Minister in writing on ceasing to meet a remission criterion` TRUE 30) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person` `inform the Minister in writing that a remission criterion is no longer satisfied` 10)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 8(2) -- tell the Minister in writing on ceasing to meet a remission criterion` FALSE 30) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL 31)) EQUALS FULFILLED

#TRACE `s 8(2) -- tell the Minister in writing on ceasing to meet a remission criterion` TRUE 30 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 31)
-- expect: BREACH by `the person`: s 8(2), maximum penalty $2 500

-- s 8(3): inform on day 5, refund $255.60 on day 40, within the (illustrative) 30 and 60 days.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 8(3), (4) -- tell the Minister and refund a payment not entitled to` 255.60 30 60) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person` `inform the Minister in writing of a payment the person was not entitled to receive` 5), (EVENT `the person` (`refund the payment to the Minister` 255.60) 40)) EQUALS FULFILLED

#TRACE `s 8(3), (4) -- tell the Minister and refund a payment not entitled to` 255.60 30 60 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person` DOES `inform the Minister in writing of a payment the person was not entitled to receive` AT 5
    PARTY `the person` DOES `refund the payment to the Minister` 100 AT 40
    (WAITUNTIL 61)
-- expect: BREACH by `the person`: s 8(3)(b), a refund of 100 is not the 255.60 received; recoverable as a debt (s 8(4))
